{"Setting a dummy `refresh_token` string ('refresh_token') when it is absent is risky and can corrupt credentials, causing subsequent refresh attempts to fail in a non-obvious way. Should avoid mutating and rely on callers to preserve existing refresh token.": 0.9320836067199707, "The `minimumTokenResponseSchema` object shape is invalid - using `[z.string().toString()]` as computed keys creates a single property with that literal key (e.g. 'ZodString'), not an index signature over arbitrary keys. Should use `z.object({ access_token: z.string() }).passthrough()` and handle expiry fields separately.": 0.9056636095046997, "`parseRefreshTokenResponse` returns a wrapper object (`{ success, data }`) but is used where `googleCredentialSchema.parse` was, which returned the parsed credential object directly. This will write the wrapper into `credential.key`, breaking callers that expect it to match `googleCredentialSchema`.": 0.9431257247924805, "Mixing response types between the sync endpoint and `refreshFunction` will break callers - returns a `fetch` `Response` when sync is enabled but Axios/SDK results otherwise. Callers expecting `.data` or specific shapes will hit runtime errors when sync-path returns bare `Response`.": 0.9268390536308289}